<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aisha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 614–678 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aisha bint Abi Bakr was a wife of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophet-muhammad">Prophet Muhammad</a> and daughter of the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>, Abu Bakr. She was an important transmitter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadith">hadith</a> and a respected religious authority. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-fitna">First Fitna</a> she opposed the caliph Ali and was defeated at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-camel">Battle of the Camel</a> in 656, part of the civil strife that marked the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a>.</p></div>
